# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true by default) rewrites the
# working tree to CRLF, and two things break in ways that do not name their
# cause:
#
#   - Prettier's endOfLine defaults to "lf", so `bun run format:check` reports
#     EVERY file in the repo as misformatted. The real diff is then impossible
#     to see, and "just run format --write" fights the checkout forever.
#
#   - Vite's shebang stripper removes `#!...` but leaves the trailing `\r`, so
#     `scripts/devcontainer-open.mjs` fails to load under vitest with a bare
#     "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" pointing at nothing. The same
#     file imports fine under plain node, which makes it a genuinely confusing
#     hour. See scripts/devcontainer-open.test.mjs.
#
# Nothing here is a preference about editors. It is the setting that makes the
# checks mean the same thing on Windows as they do in the dev container.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, never touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
